### api/incidents — incident history (M6, docs/m6-plan.md §3.10)
#
# Read-only: the worker's evaluator opens and closes incidents. Run auth.http's
# register + login first. An incident appears once an endpoint has failed
# failureThreshold times in a row (default 3) -- point one at a port nothing
# listens on, or see docs/m6-verification.md for a target that can be switched
# down and up. Replace :id with real ids.

@baseUrl = {{$dotenv baseUrl}}

###
# @name listIncidents
# 200, newest first (openedAt DESC). openedAt is the FIRST failed probe of the
# run, confirmedAt the one that reached the threshold: detectionLatencyMs is
# the difference. durationMs is null while open.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/incidents

###
# @name listOpenIncidents
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/incidents?status=open

###
# @name listClosedIncidentsPage
# The cursor is the last incident's id from the previous page. limit is capped
# by MAX_LIST_LIMIT, not rejected above it.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/incidents?status=closed&limit=10&cursor=:lastId

###
# @name getIncident
# 200. cause is the first failed probe's evidence, copied when the incident
# opened: class, code, statusCode, and which assertion failed (assertion).
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/incidents/:id

###
# @name endpointIncidents
# D-5 / FR-27: one endpoint's history.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/endpoints/:id/incidents

###
# @name serviceIncidents
# D-5: every endpoint of one service.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/services/:id/incidents?status=open

###
# @name incidentNotFound
# 404 NOT_FOUND -- byte-identical for an id that does not exist, one that is
# another user's, and one whose endpoint was deleted.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/incidents/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000

###
# @name incidentBadStatus
# 400 VALIDATION_FAILED: status is open or closed.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/incidents?status=broken

###
# @name incidentBadId
# 400 BAD_REQUEST: the id is not a UUID.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/incidents/not-a-uuid
